\subsubsection{Simple English Wikipedia}
\citet{kauchak2011sentence} have constructed a dataset of over 1,700 examples of sentences and their corresponding simplified versions from Simple English Wikipedia (SEW) and English Wikipedia (EW) for the purpose of sentence simplification.

\paragraph{Task}
Given a sentence from SEW, predict the simplified text of that sentence from the corresponding sentence in EW.

\subsection{Paraphrase Datasets}
\label{sec:paraphrase-datasets}

\noindent \textbf{Ground Truth:} from chongqing became a municipality of the People's Republic of china

\noindent \textbf{Baseline:} \textit{the People's Republic of china became a municipality of the republic of china}


\noindent\textbf{Input:} Please simplify the following text to improve its readability, ensuring its core meaning remains intact: 'from chongqing became a municipality of the republic of china.' Provide only the simplified text as the response.



\item \textit{Source}:  'Bruce Springsteen and the E Street Band have announced that they'll perform at the first-ever MLB game at Citi Field on Sept. 4.'

\textbf{\textit{Target}}: 'The E Street Band and Bruce Springsteen will perform at the MLB's first ever game at Citi Field.'

\textbf{\textit{Response}}:  \textit{A famous band will perform at a sports match.}

\subsection{Flickr8K}
Flickr8k \cite{hodosh2013framing} consists of 8,000 Flickr images. Each image has 5 captions written by humans and in average each caption has 124 words. Each caption has 5 different keywords. The goal is to generate image descriptions, where the model needs to predict the 5 captions that describe an image. The evaluation metric is the Mean-Reciprocal-Rank (MRR) score and the success rate is set to be at least 50\%.

